(7662298, 1248815, 96574, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Beaubeau:</b></div><hr/><i> Very nicely done. I would love to see this photograph with less depth of field and the hero on an angle rather than sideways. I think it would showcase the main subject if the other items were a little less in focus.  Also the fork should play a more active role...Sorry but I do a lot of food photography and these are just my opinions. But I do Love the photo and it looks yummy. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the constructive criticisms and advice on the image.  I don''t do too many of these food or product type shots so I''m kind of lost trying to do food styling.  I''m sure I''ll make more cheesecakes so can experiment with different compositions.  :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2020-05-12 01:50:38.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Beaubeau: Very nicely done. I would love to see this photograph with less depth of field and the hero on an angle rather than sideways. I think it would showcase the main subject if the other items were a little less in focus.  Also the fork should play a more active role...Sorry but I do a lot of food photography and these are just my opinions. But I do Love the photo and it looks yummy.   Thanks for the constructive criticisms and advice on the image.  I don''t do too many of these food or product type shots so I''m kind of lost trying to do food styling.  I''m sure I''ll make more cheesecakes so can experiment with different compositions.  :)', '2020-05-11 14:44:39.000000', '2020-05-12 02:50:38.000000', 0),
