(7662401, 1248786, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by primabarbara:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by primabarbara:</b></div><hr/><i> Roz - huge Congrats! <br/>I''m looking for a hat as dinner right now... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ohh your comment makes me want to explain it...<br/> <br/>In German, if we are quite sure something is going to happen, we say: Ich fresse einen Besen wenn.." which literally means: "I''ll eat a broom, if..."<br/>But I was pretty sure noboy would understand that so I was looking on an internet site for English idioms what might have a similar meaning and I got the suggestion: "I''ll eat my hat if..."<br/>Since I predicted a <b>blue </b>in my first comment during voting but your picture ended up with a <b>yellow </b> ribbon I felt obliged to say in a funny way that my prediciton didn''t come true and now I should make my announcement (eating my hat) come true. That''s it. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>lol .. i should have realized .. but i didnt follow the train of thought .. i''m looking for a hat as dinner right now .. ie. i''ll eat my hat .. <br/>anyway .. thankyou for clearing that up .. and if you predict a blue, red or yellow in the future and i dont get it .. i will totally understand if you say you''ll be looking for a hat as dinner .. you could always say broom as well .. i would understand altho a lot of non-german speaking ppl may not .. <br/>so funny .. xx</td>', 'Originally posted by primabarbara: Originally posted by primabarbara: Roz - huge Congrats! I''m looking for a hat as dinner right now...   Ohh your comment makes me want to explain it... In German, if we are quite sure something is going to happen, we say: Ich fresse einen Besen wenn.." which literally means: "I''ll eat a broom, if..."But I was pretty sure noboy would understand that so I was looking on an internet site for English idioms what might have a similar meaning and I got the suggestion: "I''ll eat my hat if..."Since I predicted a blue in my first comment during voting but your picture ended up with a yellow  ribbon I felt obliged to say in a funny way that my prediciton didn''t come true and now I should make my announcement (eating my hat) come true. That''s it.   lol .. i should have realized .. but i didnt follow the train of thought .. i''m looking for a hat as dinner right now .. ie. i''ll eat my hat .. anyway .. thankyou for clearing that up .. and if you predict a blue, red or yellow in the future and i dont get it .. i will totally understand if you say you''ll be looking for a hat as dinner .. you could always say broom as well .. i would understand altho a lot of non-german speaking ppl may not .. so funny .. xx', '2020-05-12 18:22:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7662409, 1248383, 115664, '<td valign="top">Okay. These are three orphaned Great Horned Owlets. We currently have 5, plus 3 Barred owlets and 3 Screech owlets. We also have 2 Pileated woodpecker chicks and a Blue Jay chick. On the mammal side we have an orphaned baby beaver and an orphaned baby red fox cub! As you can imagine it is more like a full time job than a hobby, but I love it! :-)<br/>My husband is a licensed wildlife rehabilitator and has the only migratory bird license in the state of Arkansas. He is also a vet! Only one person per household is allowed to hold the license but I have WAY more hours than are required to have my own. I am assured that if anything were to happen to my husband I would be given a license. Last year we built a flight cage that is large enough for eagles to fly in. We call it the Creathedral since it resembles a cathedral is is just as huge! :-)</td>', 'Okay. These are three orphaned Great Horned Owlets. We currently have 5, plus 3 Barred owlets and 3 Screech owlets. We also have 2 Pileated woodpecker chicks and a Blue Jay chick. On the mammal side we have an orphaned baby beaver and an orphaned baby red fox cub! As you can imagine it is more like a full time job than a hobby, but I love it! :-)My husband is a licensed wildlife rehabilitator and has the only migratory bird license in the state of Arkansas. He is also a vet! Only one person per household is allowed to hold the license but I have WAY more hours than are required to have my own. I am assured that if anything were to happen to my husband I would be given a license. Last year we built a flight cage that is large enough for eagles to fly in. We call it the Creathedral since it resembles a cathedral is is just as huge! :-)', '2020-05-12 21:51:38.000000', NULL, 0),
