(7662935, 1248671, 30049, '<td valign="top">Darn it.  Meant to come back to address this comment made by <img alt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=3306" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">GolferDDS</a> and just lost track of time.<br/> <br/><i>"...  I wish you had taken the picture at a different angle and in total focus to show the entire subject that represents your talent."</i> <br/> <br/>While I do appreciate the comment and opinion I wanted to treat this challenge as a photo contest first, hobby item second.  With this in mind I went with the eye and head in focus and the balance resolving to bokeh.  Thought this was a bit more "artistic" than just doing a product shot.  :-)</td>', 'Darn it.  Meant to come back to address this comment made by  GolferDDS and just lost track of time. "...  I wish you had taken the picture at a different angle and in total focus to show the entire subject that represents your talent."  While I do appreciate the comment and opinion I wanted to treat this challenge as a photo contest first, hobby item second.  With this in mind I went with the eye and head in focus and the balance resolving to bokeh.  Thought this was a bit more "artistic" than just doing a product shot.  :-)', '2020-05-18 13:09:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7664521, 1248879, 91360, '<td valign="top">excellent shot for the challenge. I think that the eyes should point the camera in kind of kinky way..:) (top 1 for me in that challenge)<br/></td>', 'excellent shot for the challenge. I think that the eyes should point the camera in kind of kinky way..:) (top 1 for me in that challenge)', '2020-05-30 10:45:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7664559, 1248879, 253397, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ytshuva:</b></div><hr/><i> excellent shot for the challenge. I think that the eyes should point the camera in kind of kinky way..:) (top 1 for me in that challenge) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There were a few like that, but for some reason they just did not work. <br/>Maybe because once I look in the camera the eyes start competing with all the many things around them for attention. <br/>Or maybe I did not like the expression, who knows. <br/>This one was me trying to figure out if the old wireless shutter my hand will work with the new camera. <br/>Worrying, and you can kinda tell, that it is not working and all the set up would be for nothing. <br/>The pinned on yarn balls were sliding ever so slightly the whole time. :D</td>', 'Originally posted by ytshuva: excellent shot for the challenge. I think that the eyes should point the camera in kind of kinky way..:) (top 1 for me in that challenge)   There were a few like that, but for some reason they just did not work. Maybe because once I look in the camera the eyes start competing with all the many things around them for attention. Or maybe I did not like the expression, who knows. This one was me trying to figure out if the old wireless shutter my hand will work with the new camera. Worrying, and you can kinda tell, that it is not working and all the set up would be for nothing. The pinned on yarn balls were sliding ever so slightly the whole time. :D', '2020-05-30 17:14:40.000000', NULL, 0);
